{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers","id":1099032,"title":"legal penalty for murdering sleepers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T23:03:08-07:00","id":1099032,"title":"legal penalty for murdering sleepers?","content":"the protocols say &quot;protect the sleepers,they are ignorant of what they do&quot; so i always assumed that at the very least,sacrificing some random entirely innocent guy for quintessence is illegal&quot; yet what is the penalty for it? note,getting on the bad side of the golden chalice doesn't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T23:32:39-07:00","id":1099035,"title":"","content":"Depends on the local Chantry, you might get a branding or exile at best or executed at worst. Some might even toss you in sleeper jail or hand you over to the technocratic union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T23:46:59-07:00","id":1099039,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, also, that if a mage goes around sacrificing people to harvest their delicious Quintessence, it's going to raise questions over whether said mage has Fallen, or become an Infernalist. Nephandi and Infernalists do the human sacrifice thing all the time.<br /> <br /> So if this becomes a regular thing for the character, they're in serious danger of getting sanctioned for execution, if not Gilgul.<br /> <br /> Even if they a tribunal doesn't conclude they've Fallen, the character has still been murdering tons of people for personal gain. Probably fallen into a Morbid Quiet, or wracked up loads of Jhor Resonance. That stuff isn't subtle, man. I'd half expect the Euthanatos to send someone to assassinate them, if it gets really bad. We can't have another Voormas potentially running around, plotting the doom of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T00:17:39-07:00","id":1099047,"title":"","content":"It really depends on who finds out and when and if there are mitigating circumstances. a Verbena practicing the old bloody ways to replenish the land that's been drained might have mitigating circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T00:25:03-07:00","id":1099048,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure those are willing participants, lest the nature of the sacrifice taint the land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:12:18-07:00","id":1099053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099048#post1099048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure those are willing participants, lest the nature of the sacrifice taint the land.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the sort of thing you need to investigate when you hear &quot;Mage sacrifices sleeper for power&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:40:35-07:00","id":1099068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099053#post1099053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the sort of thing you need to investigate when you hear &amp;quot;Mage sacrifices sleeper for power&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just get ready to run if they ask you to stay for the harvest festival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T03:02:20-07:00","id":1099089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the local Chantry, you might get a branding or exile at best or executed at worst. Some might even toss you in sleeper jail or hand you over to the technocratic union.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Unless it was a massive fuck up that affected the Traditions as a whole it's likely to stay in Chantry, and these punishments seem appropiate. The punishment could include the confiscation of Quintessence, or other magical goods, and Censure. If the crime was committed to gain power, stripping that power seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Also it's worth to note that different Traditions have codes, and special punishments, that may apply. I remember somewhere that Hermetics have to compensate the sleeper victims (or, in this case, it's family) somehow-I think this was in the Trad Book, as part of the peripheral code, not the central one. An Extatic may have to bear the suffering of the family (using Mind), as experimenting the suffering you caused it's a common punishment within the trad. The Golden Chalice may visit anyone, but the Council of Ethic of the Etherites deals exclusively with their members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:42:21-07:00","id":1099249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099039#post1099039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd half expect the Euthanatos to send someone to assassinate them, if it gets really bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, most of the Traditions have their own internal &quot;secret police&quot; created to handle this sort of thing without having to rely on intervention by outsiders. The Akashic Black Hat Society, the Verbena's Silver Blade, House Quaesitor, the Etherite Council for Scientific Ethics, etc. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:31:11-07:00","id":1099266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099249#post1099249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, most of the Traditions have their own internal &quot;secret police&quot; created to handle this sort of thing without having to rely on intervention by outsiders. The Akashic Black Hat Society, the Verbena's Silver Blade, House Quaesitor, the Etherite Council for Scientific Ethics, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be that as it may, it depends on which book you're reading. At least among the Houses of Hermes, after the virtual destruction of House Janissary, the Euthanatos (who, incidentally, were largely responsible for Janissary's decimation) took on the role of police. Quaesitor might be the <i>judges</i> of Hermes, but, lacking an internal group to enforce those judgments, the Euthanatos had to fill that role. It is a state of affairs few are happy with, but they have the skills to investigate corruption (especially Jhor-corruption), and put an end to them. They are also an outside third party, which make them politically expedient for the mire that is the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> Even were that not the case, they'd investigate - and intervene - anyway. That might mean turning over evidence to the given Tradition's own authorities, or by taking matters into their own hands.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that, if a mage happens to be killing people regularly - without it being willing victims - just to gain Quintessence or other forms of power, it's easier perhaps to ask forgiveness than permission. A target of summery execution is not necessarily going to be sympathetic in that case, so long as the evidence can be presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:42:03-07:00","id":1099271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099266#post1099266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> lacking an internal group to enforce those judgments,</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like a House founded on Zoroastrian ideas of the eternal battle of Light, Truth and Purity against the forces of Darkness, Deceit and Corruption, who master physical and mystical methods of combat in order to protect others and bring purification to the guilty with death by fire?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T16:27:10-07:00","id":1099328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099271#post1099271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like a House founded on Zoroastrian ideas of the eternal battle of Light, Truth and Purity against the forces of Darkness, Deceit and Corruption, who master physical and mystical methods of combat in order to protect others and bring purification to the guilty with death by fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't look at me. This is a development in the books. Take it up with them.<br /> <br /> Concerning the aforementioned group, House Flambaeu are war-mages. They are NOT spies, investigators, and assassins. That was House Jannisary's job. A job they obviously can't do anymore, because most of them are dead.<br /> <br /> You don't send the pyromaniacs to infiltrate a chantry, looking for signs of infernalism or human sacrifice. Because, you know, folks who engage in naughty things like that tend to want to hide them. Rooting out corruption is just not in a Flambeau's skill set. This all ignoring that Paradox tends to limit how much of that much-vaunted mystical methods of combat the magus could bring to bear.<br /> <br /> What you'd want out of a group that investigates bad stuff within the organization is skills that allow for deception, sensing intent, gathering information, and, if needed, eliminating or capturing people quietly. Things that Janissary once excelled at, and that the Euthanatos excel at now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 06-01-2017, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:21:53-07:00","id":1099360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099328#post1099328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't look at me. This is a development in the books. Take it up with them.<br /> <br /> Concerning the aforementioned group, House Flambaeu are war-mages. They are NOT spies, investigators, and assassins. That was House Jannisary's job. A job they obviously can't do anymore, because most of them are dead.<br /> <br /> You don't send the pyromaniacs to infiltrate a chantry, looking for signs of infernalism or human sacrifice. Because, you know, folks who engage in naughty things like that tend to want to hide them. Rooting out corruption is just not in a Flambeau's skill set. This all ignoring that Paradox tends to limit how much of that much-vaunted mystical methods of combat the magus could bring to bear.<br /> <br /> What you'd want out of a group that investigates bad stuff within the organization is skills that allow for deception, sensing intent, gathering information, and, if needed, eliminating or capturing people quietly. Things that Janissary once excelled at, and that the Euthanatos excel at now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't send decieving assassins to enforce a judges decision either. Quaesitor judges. Flambaeu burns those who try to defy the judgements. Seems fairly simple dynamic to me. And doesn't involve another tradition entirely policing the arrogant as fuck Order of Hermes. Because quite honestly I could see that being the source of someone starting an out and out shooting war between the two.<br /> <br /> As to the Thread premise. Murdering sleepers for their quintessence is an absolutely pointless endeavour. A sacrificed sleeper who isn't a willing sacrifice is essentially casting a low level magic spell called &quot;Fuck you and everything you stand for, you murderer.&quot; That means any quintessence that might have been gained is instead lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 06-01-2017, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:29:26-07:00","id":1099363,"title":"","content":"The Etherites don't really have a &quot;Secret&quot; police. They have a pretty standard operation procedure. Etherite 1 is grinding people down into liquid quintessence for Science. Etherite 2 is &quot;That's fucked up&quot; Finds 3 Masters of the tradition and they have a trial. Had this come up in a game the other way around where I had to prove the full sapience of a Construct and thus its rights as a person vs a machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T03:03:07-07:00","id":1099425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099089#post1099089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Unless it was a massive fuck up that affected the Traditions as a whole it's likely to stay in Chantry, and these punishments seem appropiate. The punishment could include the confiscation of Quintessence, or other magical goods, and Censure. If the crime was committed to gain power, stripping that power seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Also it's worth to note that different Traditions have codes, and special punishments, that may apply. I remember somewhere that Hermetics have to compensate the sleeper victims (or, in this case, it's family) somehow-I think this was in the Trad Book, as part of the peripheral code, not the central one. An Extatic may have to bear the suffering of the family (using Mind), as experimenting the suffering you caused it's a common punishment within the trad. The Golden Chalice may visit anyone, but the Council of Ethic of the Etherites deals exclusively with their members.</div> </div> </div> </div>i believe the hermetic book merely says that wanton murder of sleepers is a high crime. but doesn't say anything about which specific punishment applies.<br /> also while i don't remember tradition laws properly, i don't think that individual chantries can(legally) do anything worst to a mage than exiling them. i.e if being a sleeper killer for fun and profit is against their law<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 06-02-2017, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T03:04:45-07:00","id":1099426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099360#post1099360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't send decieving assassins to enforce a judges decision either. Quaesitor judges. Flambaeu burns those who try to defy the judgements. Seems fairly simple dynamic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except how does House Quaesitor get the evidence to make a proper decision? Who investigates, and in such a way that doesn't tip off the ones being investigated? Certainly not the Flambaeu mage. He comes in later, after the matter has already been looked into.<br /> <br /> And, again, I don't know what to tell you. The Euthanatos assuming fallen Janissary's role is <i>canon in the books</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T03:05:43-07:00","id":1099427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099039#post1099039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind, also, that if a mage goes around sacrificing people to harvest their delicious Quintessence, it's going to raise questions over whether said mage has Fallen, or become an Infernalist. Nephandi and Infernalists do the human sacrifice thing all the time.<br /> <br /> So if this becomes a regular thing for the character, they're in serious danger of getting sanctioned for execution, if not Gilgul.<br /> <br /> Even if they a tribunal doesn't conclude they've Fallen, the character has still been murdering tons of people for personal gain. Probably fallen into a Morbid Quiet, or wracked up loads of Jhor Resonance. That stuff isn't subtle, man. I'd half expect the Euthanatos to send someone to assassinate them, if it gets really bad. We can't have another Voormas potentially running around, plotting the doom of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>for the purpose of this question let's assume that the mage is not Fallen in any way or ridiculously infected by jhor and can genuinely claim this before a ring of truth/mindreading etc.<br /> i.e an &quot;honest&quot; bastard who is otherwise an upstanding mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T04:15:11-07:00","id":1099441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099427#post1099427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for the purpose of this question let's assume that the mage is not Fallen in any way or ridiculously infected by jhor and can genuinely claim this before a ring of truth/mindreading etc.<br /> i.e an &quot;honest&quot; bastard who is otherwise an upstanding mage</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that because most Mages are busy, and also because various Mage organizations and plots are spread thin, such a 'bastard' might get a pass or a relatively minor tell-off and/or punishment. Something along the lines of: &quot;<i>It's better you move to this state, it's been decided...oh and by the way, if you choose this city, then there just might be a Cabal there who are in need of your expertise in regards to you-know-what.&quot;</i>).<br /> In an ideal world the punishments would be more severe; but, as many Hermetics (and others) will tell you, we live in a world where more things need to be taken into account than the idealized state of matters - like politics, practical needs, and sheer Magickal power and knowledge. Let's say you want to punish an Arete 6 Mage for torturing and murdering two Sleepers. He/She has at the very least Time 4, Forces 5, Correspondence 4, and is one of the sought-after Mages with Prime 5. The Mage won't go down easily or quietly. Some Mages have his back for the time her/his actions saved an entire Cabal from a Technocracy dragnet in the days of the Pogrom; and she/he is a fine teacher of multiple Spheres. The lives of the two Sleepers can, in the end, seem insignificant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-02-2017, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T05:28:32-07:00","id":1099460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers#post1099032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the protocols say &quot;protect the sleepers,they are ignorant of what they do&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you seem to know what you're talking about<b></b>: where do the protocols say this in the original text (i.e. pre-M20)? I only found a short mention in the glossary so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:11:43-07:00","id":1099477,"title":"","content":"In the Book of the Traditions(revised) there's a whole chapter on Traditional law, including the interpretation of that Tradition. I think it's also mentioned in the basics of Mage 1rst Edition, and Second","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:50:49-07:00","id":1099494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099477#post1099477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Book of the Traditions(revised) there's a whole chapter on Traditional law, including the interpretation of that Tradition. I think it's also mentioned in the basics of Mage 1rst Edition, and Second</div> </div> </div> </div>Guide to the Traditions 166 and onward. Thanks! White Wolf index turns out unhelpful once again. -_-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:58:34-07:00","id":1099496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099426#post1099426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except how does House Quaesitor get the evidence to make a proper decision? Who investigates, and in such a way that doesn't tip off the ones being investigated? Certainly not the Flambaeu mage. He comes in later, after the matter has already been looked into.<br /> <br /> And, again, I don't know what to tell you. The Euthanatos assuming fallen Janissary's role is <i>canon in the books</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quaesitori <i>can</i> investigate - they did so before Janissary, are noted as still doing so in cases of Infernalism, it's pretty much the reason for the exception in the rules about spying on Hermetics, and the Revised House's Goal is &quot;Preservation and, now, enforcement of Hermetic law&quot;, and it notes that they're initiating law enforcement professionals to fill the gap.<br /> <br /> I believe that the Euthanatos's post-Janissary role is the <i>Traditions' </i>internal police force (see EuthRev), not the internal police force of <i>the Order of Hermes? </i>Post-Janissary it looks to me like the Quaesitors are dusting off their 300-year-old detective hats, if OoHRevised is to be believed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099460#post1099460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you seem to know what you're talking about<b></b>: where do the protocols say this in the original text (i.e. pre-M20)? I only found a short mention in the glossary so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been in the Protocols in Mage 1st and 2nd. I vaguely recall that Revised omits the full list of Protocols - among the many concessions that had to be made to space in that tome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T10:41:20-07:00","id":1099570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099460#post1099460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you seem to know what you're talking about<b></b>: where do the protocols say this in the original text (i.e. pre-M20)? I only found a short mention in the glossary so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i think it's found in uide to the traditions and mage the sorcerer'scrusade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T11:13:55-07:00","id":1099586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099328#post1099328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't send the pyromaniacs to infiltrate a chantry, looking for signs of infernalism or human sacrifice. Because, you know, folks who engage in naughty things like that tend to want to hide them. Rooting out corruption is just not in a Flambeau's skill set. This all ignoring that Paradox tends to limit how much of that much-vaunted mystical methods of combat the magus could bring to bear.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>In the Order of Hermes, the Hermetic Code is represented by two </i><i>separate yet equally important Houses: Guernicus<sup>1</sup>, who investigate crime; and Flambeau, who incinerate the offenders. These are their stories. </i><br /> <br /> And no, I'm not picking at you. Like you say, some of the stuff in the books (especially in the lead up to Time of Judgment) was a bit wonky. Besides, I just enjoy the idea of having a pair of Hermetics doing the mismatched buddy cop thing from the 80s and 90s.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I prefer Guernicus over Quaesitor, as it leaves the title of Quaesitor open as a House or even Tradition wide role of investigator that any character can take up.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T11:17:50-07:00","id":1099588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099363#post1099363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Etherites don't really have a &quot;Secret&quot; police.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a secret one, no. But their rules enforcement group is noted in Book of Madness Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T12:15:31-07:00","id":1099606,"title":"","content":"Etherites do actually have a secret police/secret agent branch. Notable in that they are generally armed with dart guns full of hallucinogens rather than lethal weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T15:37:38-07:00","id":1099666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099606#post1099606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etherites do actually have a secret police/secret agent branch. Notable in that they are generally armed with dart guns full of hallucinogens rather than lethal weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shh! We aren't supposed to talk about the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Final_Programme_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Cornelius Commandos</a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T00:39:27-07:00","id":1099771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099441#post1099441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that because most Mages are busy, and also because various Mage organizations and plots are spread thin, such a 'bastard' might get a pass or a relatively minor tell-off and/or punishment. Something along the lines of: &quot;<i>It's better you move to this state, it's been decided...oh and by the way, if you choose this city, then there just might be a Cabal there who are in need of your expertise in regards to you-know-what.&quot;</i>).<br /> In an ideal world the punishments would be more severe; but, as many Hermetics (and others) will tell you, we live in a world where more things need to be taken into account than the idealized state of matters - like politics, practical needs, and sheer Magickal power and knowledge. Let's say you want to punish an Arete 6 Mage for torturing and murdering two Sleepers. He/She has at the very least Time 4, Forces 5, Correspondence 4, and is one of the sought-after Mages with Prime 5. The Mage won't go down easily or quietly. Some Mages have his back for the time her/his actions saved an entire Cabal from a Technocracy dragnet in the days of the Pogrom; and she/he is a fine teacher of multiple Spheres. The lives of the two Sleepers can, in the end, seem insignificant...</div> </div> </div> </div>so basically a million is just a statistic and a few sleepers do not even make it into the stats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T05:58:11-07:00","id":1099796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099427#post1099427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for the purpose of this question let's assume that the mage is not Fallen in any way or ridiculously infected by jhor and can genuinely claim this before a ring of truth/mindreading etc.<br /> i.e an &quot;honest&quot; bastard who is otherwise an upstanding mage</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to present mage societies as being fairly small (less than 20 mages per side per city) and running on social contract rather than codified rules. A mage who kills people will be shunned and ostracised even if his actions are justified (e.g. murder of technocrats). He'd be dealt with in some way up to and including execution if the mage's actions endanger the mage society (public sacrifices, trails of clues, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T07:31:51-07:00","id":1099817,"title":"","content":"Personally I tend towards the opposite. While individual cabals are relatively small 5-6 people at most on average, you have dozens upon dozens of them in any given city. While the Technocracy has a presence depending upon the location of the city in question and directly proportional to the overall traditional presence. Hotbeds of Deviancy have more agents than relatively stable locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T00:30:24-07:00","id":1100036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099032-legal-penalty-for-murdering-sleepers?p=1099606#post1099606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etherites do actually have a secret police/secret agent branch. Notable in that they are generally armed with dart guns full of hallucinogens rather than lethal weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Shadow Ministry is counter intelligence. Honestly I'd argue most Traditions don't have &quot;Secret&quot; police. They have just you know Police.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}